What are Self-driving Sanitation Boats?
Self-driving sanitation boats are autonomous or remotely operated vessels designed for surface cleaning and waste collection in water bodies. These AI-powered systems combine navigation sensors, computer vision, and robotic collection mechanisms to remove floating debris, oil slicks, and algae blooms without human intervention. Their primary deployment areas include urban rivers, harbors, reservoirs, and recreational water spaces where traditional cleaning methods prove inefficient or costly.
